<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.arios4k.Voltkit</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>Voltkit</name>
  <summary>Power tools for your Linux desktop in one app</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.arios4k">
    <name>Alexis Rios-Negron</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Voltkit brings everyday desktop tools to Linux in one GTK4 and libadwaita app and a
      single command, built for Wayland with global hotkeys.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Screen OCR: copy the text from any part of the screen</li>
      <li>A QR code scanner and maker</li>
      <li>A screen color picker with contrast checking, and a screen ruler</li>
      <li>An image and video compressor that strips metadata</li>
      <li>A text expander with a snippet picker, and Smart Paste for pasting the clipboard converted</li>
      <li>Keep Awake, and a hosts and environment variable editor</li>
      <li>A finder for the apps keeping a drive, file or port busy</li>
      <li>An app permissions manager and a troubleshooter for sleep and wake-ups</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
